                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5d730e4-4f8c-374f-9cfe-a6424954863a",
                                        "entry_id": "ae62c621-c11b-3114-835b-5e925a79ce30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to heaven or to the sky; celestial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31d1e1a5-d928-472a-b005-f944ea6f4bbc",
                                                "sense_id": "c5d730e4-4f8c-374f-9cfe-a6424954863a",
                                                "text": "[…]and there, after due prayers to the gods who dwell in ether supernal, had taken solemn counsel whereby they might, if so be it might be, bring once more into honour among mortal men the winged speech of the seadivided Gael."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "240fba36-b033-35dc-8474-1789db0d27c5",
                                        "entry_id": "ae62c621-c11b-3114-835b-5e925a79ce30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exalted, exquisite, superlative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42cd2c9b-55bf-4589-a3e0-8ee32cf49772",
                                                "sense_id": "240fba36-b033-35dc-8474-1789db0d27c5",
                                                "text": "Even the sunlight assumed a supernal glamour, as if some special atmosphere or exhalation mantled the whole region."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8d26698-f63f-4619-92ae-fb33978dc554",
                                                "sense_id": "240fba36-b033-35dc-8474-1789db0d27c5",
                                                "text": "Pig, not normally reticent in these matters, now acted like a mystic after a vision; unable, maybe unwilling, to put in words this ineffable or supernal talent of Panky’s."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cd218ee-ce0a-4955-a35d-f2bb4c37fbae",
                                                "sense_id": "240fba36-b033-35dc-8474-1789db0d27c5",
                                                "text": "For what did Cauchy know, or Christoffel,\nOr Fourier, or any Boole or Euler,\nWielding their compasses, their pens and rulers,\nOf thy supernal sinusoidal spell?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
